    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The full-stack change is complete and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented client contacts (name, email, role) as an additive full-stack change, following the codebase's conventions (modeled on the existing projects feature).\n\n**Database** \u2014 `src/main/resources/db/migration/V12__contacts.sql`: new `contact` table (`id`, `client_id` FK \u2192 `client`, `name`, `email`, `role`), IDENTITY id like the other domain tables.\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor + Spring)**:\n- `Contact.java` \u2014 JPA entity for the `contact` table.\n- `ContactRepository.java` \u2014 Spring Data repo with `findAllByOrderByIdAsc()`.\n- `ContactsGet.java` + `contacts.GET.yml` \u2014 `GET /api/contacts` lists all contacts, oldest first.\n- `ContactsPost.java` + `contacts.POST.yml` \u2014 `POST /api/contacts` validates name/email/role and an existing client, saves, and records a `CONTACT_CREATED \u2026` line through the `Audit` service (per CLAUDE.md's side-effect rule).\n- `NewContact.java` \u2014 `@RequestBody` payload.\n- `TestSupportController.java` \u2014 extended `reset` to `TRUNCATE \u2026 RESTART IDENTITY` the `contact` table and `seed` to insert `contacts` from the fixture via `JdbcTemplate` using the fixture's explicit ids.\n\n**Front-end (additive, new files only)**:\n- `features/contacts/ClientContactsPanel.tsx` \u2014 reads `['contacts']` via `useQuery`, filters to the handed `clientId`, renders `client-contacts-table` with `contact-row-<id>` (each holding `contact-name`, `contact-email`, `contact-role`), plus an add form (`contact-form-name/-email/-role/-submit`) that mutates and `invalidateQueries(['contacts'])`.\n- `features/contacts/contacts.slot.tsx` \u2014 fills the existing `ClientDetail` slot (order 20), so nothing existing was edited.\n\nAll `data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly; both `@core` tests pass. No pinned scaffolding or the spec was touched.",
